From: dinadur <59811564+dinadur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:50:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] B70: drop leaked planning text from product answers

3 of 288 captured Telegram product answers (2026-10-07 and 10-09) contained
the model's working notes ("Need maybe ...", "Let's craft final ...") and
earlier drafts before the real answer. They passed validation because they
cite the evidence. The local model sometimes ends its thinking early and
keeps planning in the visible answer.

Quality-first validation now detects planning lines and keeps the last
draft that starts with a conclusion opener (Bottom line, Conclusion,
Recommendation, Best pick, ...) and has no planning after it; that draft then
goes through the usual checks. With no clean final draft, the answer fails
with planning_text_leaked. The three real cases keep 469, 709 and 1,610 of
1,698, 2,724 and 5,096 words; no other captured answer is flagged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
